    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Parts of the body",
     "texto": [
      "When it is clear whose body part it is, Spanish usually uses **el, la, los, las** and not «my» or «your»: **levanta la mano**, **tengo las piernas cansadas**, **me duele la espalda**.\n\n**La mano** is feminine: **la mano derecha**, **las manos frías**.\n\n**Derecho** and **izquierdo** agree with the part: **el pie derecho**, **la mano derecha**, **el brazo izquierdo**, **la pierna izquierda**.\n\n**El dedo** serves for hand and foot: **los dedos de la mano**, **los dedos del pie**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The article and the side",
     "texto": [
      "Two ideas for talking about the body:\n\n- With body parts you use **the article**, not the possessive: **Levanto la mano**, **Me duele la cabeza**. The pronoun (**me**, **te**) already says whose it is.\n- **Derecho** and **izquierdo** agree: **el pie derecho**, **la mano izquierda**, **los ojos verdes**.\n\nThe word **mano** is feminine: **la mano**, **las manos**."
     ],
